WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.530
Oh no! Mitsuki's pendant
has been stolen!

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.600
Gosh, I know you're excited about
seeing Eichi, but you can't be so careless!

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:13.100
Thanks to the stupidity of the thieves,
we ended up getting back the pendant.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Takuto... The thing you said to Mitsuki...
Did you really mean it?

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.930
So, I wonder what's going to
happen today...

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.630
Got that?

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:29.730
Yes.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:04.900
Takuto!

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:09.230
A-All right.
I'll give it back, so forgive me!

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:11.830
Here you go!

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.460
Damn it!

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.100
Takuto!

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:25.130
What an idiot.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:32.660
What do I do?

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.160
Takuto is... Takuto is...

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.400
What're you crying for,
you little loser?

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.900
You're so stupid, Takuto!

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.460
Takuto?

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:54.700
Stupid, stupid, stupid!

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.330
What's that for?!
Aren't you happy?!

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:01.730
I am happy! But why did you
do such a reckless thing?!

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.400
Takuto?

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:08.930
Why? Why do you always act so tough?
You did such a dangerous thing!

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.860
Oh, enough, enough!

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.900
Answer me, Takuto!

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.600
Why should I, you little loser?

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:15.730
What did you say?!

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:20.160
Takuto!

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:24.930
I-It's... It's because I like you,
of course!

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.000
Takuto...

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:56.060
I like you too!
I like you a lot Takuto!

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:57.660
Mitsuki?

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.060
Because you're such
a precious friend of mine!

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:03.260
Huh?

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:07.560
That's why it's only natural that I worry when
you do something as reckless as that!

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:09.530
Don't ever do it again!

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:11.460
Th-That's not it!

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:12.160
What?

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:21.130
Takuto?

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.030
That's right!
We're your friends!

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:24.800
Yup!

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:26.600
Miss?

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.260
Are you all right?

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:33.330
Yes! Oh, and we found
the pendant we were looking for!

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.800
That's good.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:42.230
By the way, I don't see your friend,
but where did he go?

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:48.560
Takuto said he was hungry,
and he went ahead.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:51.230
Mitsuki!

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.860
Ms. Oshige, Dr. Wakaoji!

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:56.700
Mitsuki, are you all right?!

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:00.430
Are you okay?
You didn't get hurt, did you?

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.060
No, I'm all right.

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:04.100
We were really worried!

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.930
Don't do anything like this
ever again, okay?

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:10.730
I'll need more than one heart if I'm
gonna be this close to a heart attack!

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:15.530
I'm sorry, but I really wanted
to get this pendant back.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.330
I know. It's from Eichi, isn't it?

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:22.130
But please don't ever do
anything like this again.

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:23.230
Got that?

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:23.930
Yes!

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:26.360
Takuto...

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:35.200
We had originally planned to stop by
yesterday, but it should be all right.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:36.630
How close are we?

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:38.300
We're almost there.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.760
Isn't it pretty?

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:18.330
The temperature is a lot different from
Eagle Valley, so you need to be careful.

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:19.460
I will!

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.000
<i>We're finally here.</i>

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:41.300
<i>Eichi, I'm so close</i>
<i>to you right now.</i>

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:50.100
<i>So Takuto really</i>
<i>does like Mitsuki.</i>

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:10.430
According to my notes, the person
who found a family for Eichi lives here.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:19.960
I wonder if they're out.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:27.230
No one seems to be here.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:30.660
What?! We're only one day late.
Why?

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:31.930
No way...

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:36.030
It's all right. Why don't we
just find Eichi on our own?

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:39.330
Yeah! We've come
this close to finding Eichi.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:40.730
Keep your head up!

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:42.730
Yes!

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:57.100
Hey, shouldn't we look
for him with them?

00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:58.730
I'm tired!

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:03.560
Then why don't we go to that lake
we saw earlier? It was really pretty!

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:04.260
I don't wanna go.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.160
Oh, then let's have
lunch or something.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:07.860
I don't wanna eat.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:09.130
Then...

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.660
Just leave me alone!

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:21.600
<i>So Takuto laughed and played it off earlier,</i>
<i>but were those Takuto's true feelings?</i>

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:26.760
<i>It's because I like you,</i>
<i>of course!</i>

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.500
<i>No way! There's no way!</i>
<i>That can't be the case!</i>

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:33.530
<i>Because if it is,</i>
<i>that would mean...</i>

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:38.600
<i>Unrequited love for sure?!</i>

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:41.360
<i>N-No!</i>
<i>I can't think negatively!</i>

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:45.160
<i>Even if his confession</i>
<i>were true,</i>

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.360
<i>Takuto may have totally</i>
<i>given up after being rejected!</i>

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.530
Meroko? What're you doing?

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.560
I've been watching you for a while,
but are you practicing your funny faces?

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.430
You really look like you're
having fun. I'm envious.

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:00.000
Wh-Whose fault do you think...

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:00.760
Huh?

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:05.630
You should talk. You know, nothing gets
done when you mope around.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:08.030
Just because you got rejected.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:15.660
H-Hey, Takuto, calm down.
I didn't see anything.

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:16.930
And I didn't hear anything either.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:22.130
Yeah! You're totally right.
There's no use in thinking about it like this.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:25.460
<i>Instead of thinking</i>
<i>about what'll happen</i>

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.530
<i>when she sees Eichi</i>
<i>and getting depressed,</i>

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:32.360
<i>I should watch them seeing each other</i>
<i>to break my attachment.</i>

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:35.060
You sometimes have good advice.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:40.430
<i>No way! Did he understand</i>
<i>a little bit of my feelings?</i>

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:42.600
Takuto...

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:44.130
So, I'm gonna go!

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:45.100
Huh?

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:52.530
Takuto? Gosh!
He has no idea how I feel!

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:55.600
Hey, come on!
Wait, Takuto!

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.230
I said, wait!

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.530
This beats me.

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:07.860
I thought we'd find him easily
after coming all the way here.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:12.500
But it's strange.
I wonder why we can't we find him?

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:15.460
Maybe it's not this town?

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:18.260
Ms. Oshige!

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:22.700
S-Sorry, Mitsuki,
I didn't mean to bring you down.

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:24.730
Yeah, I know.

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:29.000
One cappuccino and...
so what are you having?

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:31.360
Let me see...

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:34.130
E-Excuse me!

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.330
Excuse me, are you Japanese?

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:40.200
Huh? Yes, we are.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:41.360
I-If so...

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:44.000
The boy in this photograph...

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:49.700
Oh, I'm sure he's bigger now,
but his name is Eichi Sakurai.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.160
Do you know him?

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:55.630
I want to see him!
I've come from Japan to see Eichi!

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.500
Oh, no. We don't know.

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:07.000
I wonder what's with that girl.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:11.360
Just because we're Japanese?
To be asked out of the blue like that...

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:17.330
Oh, there they are!

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:18.060
Huh?

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:24.960
Mitsuki!

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:28.000
Mitsuki!

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:30.200
Mitsuki! Mitsuki!

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:52.830
How is she, Dr. Wakaoji?

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:55.760
Well, it seems her fever
has gone down.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.660
If she rests tonight,
there shouldn't be any problems.

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:01.600
We've suddenly come to a cold place,
and on top of that,

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:04.230
we searched around for Eichi, so her fatigue
has probably caught up with her.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:06.830
So it's not that her throat
has gotten worse?

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:07.960
That's not the case.

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.100
Oh, thank goodness!

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:12.430
It's not good to worry so much.

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:13.930
Okay.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:17.600
And you won't get better
on an empty stomach.

00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:19.960
I'll go pick up something to eat.

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:24.600
Stay in bed now!

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:25.560
Yes.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.530
Eichi, where are you?

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:49.760
I want to see you
as soon as possible.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:55.430
<i>Mitsuki, I've wanted</i>
<i>to see you too.</i>

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.000
<i>Eichi...</i>

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:02.730
<i>I like you.</i>

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.260
<i>It's because...</i>

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:09.260
<i>It's because I like you,</i>
<i>of course!</i>

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:14.300
<i>Why did you appear</i>
<i>in my thoughts, Takuto?</i>

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:17.530
<i>Jeez!</i>

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:20.400
<i>It's because you said that</i>
<i>so unexpectedly.</i>

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:25.230
<i>I like you too!</i>
<i>I like you a lot, Takuto!</i>

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:29.400
<i>I told him I liked him too.</i>

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:35.500
<i>Could it be that I can't find Eichi</i>
<i>because I said that to Takuto?</i>

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:41.130
<i>But, you're the only one I like, Eichi.</i>

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:48.730
<i>I can't see the stars or the moon.</i>

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:51.800
<i>It's only a little while before</i>
<i>I go back to Japan.</i>

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.630
<i>If I don't find Eichi...</i>

00:13:57.860 --> 00:14:01.000
She's really an easy girl
to figure out, isn't she?

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:05.830
Her heart is filled with
thoughts of Eichi.

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:12.960
<i>So give it up, Takuto.</i>

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:16.800
She's...

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:23.600
Hey!

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:25.400
You've gotta stay in bed!

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:29.260
But the sky looked
overcast from inside.

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:31.330
It's no different from out here!

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:35.300
But it made me feel like
I wouldn't see Eichi.

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:36.760
Just go back!

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:37.800
I don't want to!

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:40.800
I won't go back until
I can see the stars!

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:42.230
Enough already!

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:47.860
<i>That's right! Keep arguing.</i>
<i>Get really upset at each other.</i>

00:14:48.230 --> 00:14:51.530
<i>That way even Takuto</i>
<i>will give up completely.</i>

00:14:52.060 --> 00:14:52.730
But...

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:54.600
Don't give me that!

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:56.700
What if you catch a cold
and get stuck in bed?!

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.130
You won't be able to
look for Eichi!

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:03.430
But if I can't see
the stars and the moon,

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:06.430
I feel like I won't be
able to find Eichi either.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:07.460
Huh?

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:11.500
To not be able to see even
a single one today of all days...

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:16.260
It's almost as if I'm being told
Eichi's not here.

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:19.860
No.

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:24.730
Maybe it's that Eichi
doesn't want to see me.

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:29.900
And that's why he's hiding
so he won't be found.

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:32.360
If so...

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:36.130
What are you saying?!

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:38.400
Meroko...

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:41.300
It's not like you to get
so discouraged!

00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:42.100
But...

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:48.660
You believed in Eichi so much!
I bet Eichi still thinks about you!

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:50.300
You think so?

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:51.330
Yes!

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:55.030
How could you stop
believing in him?

00:15:59.060 --> 00:15:59.730
Snow...

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:00.460
Huh?

00:16:10.630 --> 00:16:13.860
It's as though the stars
are falling from the sky.

00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:20.400
I do want to see Eichi!

00:16:22.130 --> 00:16:27.330
That's the reason I came this far.
To tell him that I like him.

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:28.560
Mitsuki...

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:34.130
Takuto, Meroko, thank you.
I'll be all right.

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:38.230
I won't get depressed anymore
while we search for Eichi.

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:47.130
So your spirits are back up again.

00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:50.260
If you stay here, you'll catch a cold
so let's go back to your room.

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:51.230
Okay.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.930
Sorry, Takuto,
for persisting like that.

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:56.300
That's all right.

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:02.400
<i>Did I do it again?!</i>

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:07.860
<i>Even though, at first, I was thinking</i>
<i>it'd be great if they got in a fight.</i>

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:27.800
Hello?

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:30.200
Oh! Ms. Kazumi?!

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:35.100
What?!
Oh, yes! I understand!

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:38.760
Ms. Oshige?

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:43.660
Mitsuki! Get ready right away!
We might be able to see Eichi today!

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:49.060
Oh, Ms. Oshige, calm down.

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:50.760
You should drive a little slower.

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:52.800
Ms. Oshige! Faster!

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:54.260
Leave it to me!

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:55.430
<i>Th-This is scary!</i>

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:04.100
Now!

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:05.300
Okay!

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:06.060
Now!

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:09.400
Japan Festival?

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:14.260
Apparently the local Japanese club
holds this event once a year for everyone.

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:19.660
And the person that Ms. Kazumi
told us about apparently volunteers here.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:26.500
Huh?

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:28.700
Yes, that would be me.

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:30.400
I'm so glad!

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:33.860
Well, Kazumi Franklin told us
to come see you.

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:36.360
Oh... So it was you guys!

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:38.530
I had heard you were arriving
the day before yesterday,

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:40.460
but you didn't come so was
wondering what happened.

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:41.830
- Umm...
- Yes?

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:45.600
The Sakurais...
Where do the Sakurais live?

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:49.360
Oh, the Sakurais live over there.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:55.530
See that small town on the other shore?
It's a short distance by car from that town.

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:58.230
I've never been there,

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:00.930
but I've heard it's a house
with a large fir tree,

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:02.560
so I think you'll
recognize it right away.

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:09.630
<i>Eichi... He lives here and</i>
<i>sees this scenery everyday.</i>

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:19.100
So Mitsuki will finally
get to see Eichi!

00:19:20.860 --> 00:19:21.530
Is that all right?

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:22.830
Is what all right?

00:19:25.030 --> 00:19:27.730
When all's said and done,
all we can do is watch, right?

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:31.200
That's true,
we are Death Spirits after all.

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:37.360
I don't know much else
but to look in the handbook like this.

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:40.330
Oh no, Takuto! Look at this!

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:43.230
IARUKAS IHCIE
What?!

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:47.000
Eichi will make her death come sooner?!
What's that mean?!

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:49.900
I don't know!
But the handbook is absolute, you know!

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.500
We can't have her see Eichi!

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:55.460
Takuto!

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:59.200
For now, I'll go ahead and investigate!
Meroko, don't leave Mitsuki's side!

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:00.230
Got it?!

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:01.360
Yeah!

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:04.530
Gosh! Why's this happening
at a time like this?!

00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:19.360
<i>A huge fir tree.</i>

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:20.260
<i>That must be it!</i>

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:25.330
<i>So this is where Eichi lives?</i>

00:20:29.630 --> 00:20:31.230
<i>This looks like Eichi's room.</i>

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:41.860
<i>What is this cold feeling?</i>

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:48.430
<i>A shadow filled with the smell of death</i>
<i>surrounds this house.</i>

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:49.830
<i>Why?</i>

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:09.230
<i>Is that the Sakurai husband and wife?</i>
<i>They look really old.</i>

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:17.360
You need to put it out of your mind.
That was an unfortunate accident.

00:21:17.530 --> 00:21:18.530
But...

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:32.000
<i>N-No way!</i>

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:12.200
Takuto! What's going on?!
Is Eichi really going to hasten her death?

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:17.100
I don't know! But his name appeared
backwards in the Death Spirit Handbook!

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:20.460
Is it okay...to let her see Eichi?!

00:23:21.660 --> 00:23:26.100
She's been working so hard to
be able to see him! So... So...

00:23:27.460 --> 00:23:31.160
Next time on Full Moon:
"Eternal Snow."

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:32.630
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
